# 🎨 UI/UX Designing Case Studies & Portal Submissions

Welcome to my portfolio repository documenting the end-to-end design lifecycle for multiple UI/UX optimization assignments. This repository acts as the central storage ledger for academic evaluation, covering user research frameworks, interface layouts, and usability evaluation metrics.

---

## 📂 Repository Contents & Navigation

This repository is structured systematically to host design submissions across distinct project scopes:

*   **`Mobile_App_Wireframing_Task_Submission.docx`**  
    Complete low-fidelity interactive architectural blueprint documentation for **RouteEase** (Smart Local Commute Assistant Mobile App). Includes user personas, structural user flows, and wireframe specification grids.
*   **`Website_UI_Redesign_Final_Submission (1).pdf`**  
    A diagnostic case study targeting heuristic evaluations, color matrix configuration rules, typography hierarchies, and grid spacing optimizations for high-fidelity cross-platform views.
*   **`interactive_prototype_submission (1).pdf`** & **`.md`**  
    Detailed assignment files tracking functional animation properties, modal layout interactions, dynamic navigation triggers, and quick prototyping iterations.

---

## 🚀 Core Case Studies Overview

### 🗺️ Case Study 1: RouteEase — Mobile App Wireframing
*   **Methodology Used:** Design Thinking Framework (*Empathize, Define, Ideate, Prototype, Test*)
*   **Primary Focus:** Resolving urban navigation app overload by integrating disparate transit ticketing systems into a unified mobile checkout flow layout.
*   **Key Specs Documented:**
    *   **User Persona:** Maya Lin (26, Software Developer navigating city transit blocks).
    *   **Layout Framework:** Clear, monochrome layout specifications across 3 foundational screens (Main Search Dashboard, Route Options Matrix, Unified Ticketing Checkout Node) matching global accessibility tap targets (48x48dp).

### 💻 Case Study 2: Website UI Redesign & Evaluation
*   **Platform Context:** Heuristic gap diagnosis tracking operational friction across interactive layouts.
*   **Design Tokens Applied:**
    *   *Primary Theme:* Slate Deep Night (`#0F172A`)
    *   *Action Color:* Vibrant Accent Blue (`#2563EB`)
    *   *Success Indicator:* Active Emerald Green (`#10B981`)
    *   *Typography System:* Inter Sans-Serif Typography rules.

---

## 🛠️ Design Tools Utilized
*   **Figma Ecosystem:** Low/High-fidelity workspaces, smart micro-interactions, components variant logic, and dynamic transition testing loops.
*   **Adobe XD / InVision:** Interaction framework testing workflows.

